<title>USA: Morgan Stanley issues $1.0 bln 10-year notes.</title>
<headline>Morgan Stanley issues $1.0 bln 10-year notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue from Morgan Stanley Group Inc was priced on Friday, according to a syndicate source.</p>
<p>The deal, initially set as $500 million, was increased first to $750 million and then to $1.0 billion to meet fervent investor demand, a source said.</p>
<p>Morgan Stanley &amp; Co Inc was lead manager on the deal. Dean Witter Reynolds Inc was a co-manager.</p>
<p>BORROWER MORGAN STANLEY GROUP INC</p>
<p>AMT $1.0 BLN	 COUPON 6-7/8 PCT  MATURITY 3/01/2007</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.641  FIRST PAY DATE 9/01/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A1    YIELD 6.925 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-PLUS    SPREAD 57 BP	CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>U.S. corporate bond unit, 212 859-1672</p>
